{
 "script": "audit_verify",
 "about": "Synthetic audit logs. Each file's records are expanded with audit_verify._ev (seq counts up across files unless given) and chained with audit_verify.build_chain; link = genesis (a new chain), continue (chains to the previous file's last line) or orphan (chains to a line that is not present, as after retention deleted older files). mutate deletes or replaces one line after chaining. blocked = unfolded guard lines in <dir>/blocked.jsonl; ledger = rows in <dir>/../ledger.jsonl. special missing_dir points dir at a path that does not exist. Paths in notes are written as <dir>. Expected values are subsets (listed keys exact; lists exact in length and order).",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "a chain continues across monthly files",
   "files": [
